With my current xp formula, the xp required for the quest is still
roughly the same. But anyway, I don't understand why you think it's
important that you can't enter the quest with only xp from kills. I
can see why it should not be trivial to get enough xp for the quest,
but I don't see why that xp should have to come from potions of gain
level etc.

In case you're interested, the formula I'm using for xp above lvl 12
is: 6800 * (lev - 10)*(lev - 9)
Here's how the xp requirements compare to the original formula:
(original / new)
lvl 12: 40,000 / 40,800
lvl 13: 80,000 / 8,1600
lvl 14: 16,000 / 13,600
lvl 15: 32,000 / 20,400
lvl 16: 64,000 / 28,600
lvl 17: 128,000 / 38,100
and so on.
As you can see, it doesn't really make a big difference until after
lvl 14. In practice, even after lvl 14 it doesn't really make much
difference either; because every time you lose or gain a level from a
wraith / potion / vampire / succubus, all xp you gained between levels
is effectively wasted.


