Some good criticism of the game there. I agree with most of what you
said, particularly about the monsters not having the same game-
mechanics as the player; but I'm sure you won't be surprised to hear
that my mod will not go so far as to change all that. If I was going
to address all of those issue that you talked about, it would
essentially be a whole new game. If the dev-team did it they could
call it Nethack 4.0.0 or whatever; but if I did it myself, I wouldn't
call it nethack at all. I'd claim it for myself as a whole new
game. :)

Anyway, currently my interests are just in trying to correct what I
see as flaws in the game (and I've recently done this kind of stuff
with a couple of other games as well). I think a lot of what you
talked about would significantly change the feel of the game =96 perhaps
it would be for the best, but it is not what I'm trying to do with
this mod.

Incidentally, the source code for nethack truly looks ancient. As far
as I know, no one writes code like that anymore. I wonder if the
sentimental value of this antique code kind of discourages people from
rewriting big parts of the game.


